---
// PILLAR — Everyday Legends Foundation.
//
// ENTRANCE — TREATMENT A, the hairline head. Premier Leadership above opens on
// a display numeral and Athletic Management below opens on a photograph, so
// neither neighbour is matched; the other two A sections, Educational Leader
// and Contact, are nowhere near it.
//
// The section name is now the kicker rather than a 40px Fraunces title. That
// is not a demotion by accident — this file already carried the note that the
// LEDE is the section's display anchor and the name is the label on it, not
// the other way round. Treatment A is that sentence built.
//
// COLUMN WINDOW — A, the page default: columns 3-8.
//
// OVERLAP 3 OF 3 — a true optical outdent. The lede's FIRST LINE hangs left
// of the body edge and breaks into column 2, the kicker's column, so the two
// elements occupy the same strip instead of stacking in their own rectangles.
// It is the one overlap on the page with no contrast hazard at all — both
// sides of the boundary are the page's own ground — and it is expressed in em
// off the lede's own size, so it scales with the type and needs no
// per-breakpoint value.
//
// It carries the page's third overlap because the one originally planned for
// the blog photograph failed a pixel-level contrast check and was moved
// rather than shipped. See SectionBlog.astro.
//
// NO second outbound website link. Funnel index entry 02 already carries
// everydaylegend.com with identical visual treatment, and a duplicate button
// here would send a visitor to a destination the page already offers. The
// live margin carries the Instagram handle instead, which appears nowhere
// else on the page.
//
// COPY NOTE: paragraph 3 reads "education, sports, and community" in the
// client's source document. It is set here as "education, athletics, and
// service" per the project-wide pillars decision in CONTEXT.md, which matches
// the About copy and all three mockups. Deliberate — do not revert.
//
// NO HAND-SET grid-column ANYWHERE IN THIS FILE.
---

<section class="legends spread" id="sec-legends">
  <div class="section-head col-rule row-1">
    <h2 class="kicker">Everyday Legends Foundation</h2>
    <span class="head-rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <span class="section-numeral section-numeral--head" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
    <p class="role">Co-Founder &amp; Executive Director</p>
  </div>

  <p class="lede col-body row-2">Some of the most extraordinary people will never become household names.</p>

  <div class="body-copy col-indent row-3">
    <p>They are the educators, coaches, mentors, parents, community leaders, organizations, and young people who quietly show up, pour into others, open doors, and make their communities better.</p>

    <!-- A BEAT, not a body paragraph. Isolated on both sides at the tight
         step, and set in Obsidian against the Slate around it, so it carries
         primary weight in the opacity hierarchy without changing scale. -->
    <p class="body-beat">Everyday Legends Foundation was created to honor them&mdash;and to continue their work.</p>

    <p>Grounded in the pillars of education, athletics, and service, Everyday Legends celebrates those who create pathways for others while investing in the next generation through scholarships, youth initiatives, athletics, mentorship, community partnerships, and service.</p>
    <p>For Dr.&nbsp;McClain, the mission is deeply personal. Education, athletics, and service are not simply organizational pillars; they reflect values that have shaped the McClain family for years. Time, sacrifice, resources, and purpose have been intentionally invested in creating opportunities for young people while teaching the next generation that achievement carries a responsibility to give back.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- Live margin. Last in source order so it collapses inline after the
       copy rather than ahead of it. -->
  <aside class="margin-block col-margin row-3">
    <p class="margin-label">Instagram</p>
    <a class="margin-link margin-link--handle" href="https://www.instagram.com/everydaylegendsfoundation" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@everydaylegendsfoundation</a>
  </aside>
</section>

<style>
  /* RHYTHM: tight. Follows an abridged section and precedes the page's
     heaviest one, so it clusters upward rather than standing alone. */
  .legends{ padding-top: var(--vr-tight); }

  /* The role line is secondary to the name it sits under. */
  .legends .role{ opacity: 0.7; }

  /* OVERLAP 3 OF 3. -0.5em at the 62px lede is 31px, which reaches from the
     column-3 edge at x=260 back to x=229 — inside column 2, which runs
     142-236. The first line hangs; every line after it returns to the
     measure, which is what makes it read as an outdent rather than as a
     narrower column. */
  .legends .lede{ text-indent: -0.5em; }

  /* Handle is set lowercase, not uppercased — an @handle is a literal string
     and casing it up would misrepresent it. Sized down from the shared
     margin link so 26 characters still hold one line in the margin. */
  .margin-link--handle{
    font-size: clamp(11.5px, 0.95vw, 13px);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: none;
  }
</style>
